 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "Seventy-five countries back a new energy goal. Why does OPEC say it needs oil?"
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "At COP thirty-one in Antalya, Turkey, the hosts said on Wednesday that seventy-five countries now back their electricity pledge, Anadolu reports. The goal: electricity should cover thirty-five percent of the world's final energy use by twenty thirty-five. Reuters puts today's share at about twenty percent."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "OPEC's secretary general, Haitham Al Ghais, told the talks that electrification depends heavily on oil. Bigger power grids, he said, need more petroleum-based products and diesel-powered heavy machinery. He called electrification no cure-all, Reuters reports."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "Critics point out that the pledge does not require the extra power to be clean. Negotiators must still decide whether a call to phase out fossil fuels stays in the deal. Talks are set to end Friday, but could run longer."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will a fossil fuel phase-out make the final deal? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
