 "upload": {
  "title": "OPEC Tells COP31 Electrification Still Needs Oil #shorts",
  "description": "At COP31 in Antalya, Türkiye, the hosts said on Wednesday that 75 countries back their pledge to raise electricity's share of global final energy use to 35% by 2035 (Anadolu); Reuters puts today's share at about 20%. OPEC Secretary General Haitham Al Ghais told the talks that electrification depends heavily on oil, as bigger grids need petroleum-based products and diesel-powered machinery. Critics note the pledge does not require the extra power to be clean; talks are set to end Friday.\n\nSources: Reuters (via Al-Monitor, Yahoo News, MarketScreener), Anadolu Agency (via Hürriyet Daily News, Qazinform), TRT World (based on search-result excerpts). Map locations and country highlights are for orientation.\n\n#climate #cop31 #electrification #opec #energy",
